cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Indian-ASR-Bench: a reproducible WER benchmark for
  Indian-English ASR
message: >-
  If you use this benchmark, the released checkpoints, or the
  committed transcripts, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Shivam
    family-names: Sharma
    affiliation: Nanyang Technological University, Singapore
  - given-names: Changsong
    family-names: Liu
    affiliation: Nanyang Technological University, Singapore
repository-code: https://github.com/theshivam7/indian-asr-bench
url: https://huggingface.co/theshivam7
abstract: >-
  Nine ASR systems spanning four architecture classes, evaluated
  on three Indian-English corpora of contrasting design
  (TIE_shorts, Svarah, and the Indian subset of AESRC2020) under
  one registry-driven pipeline. Reports corpus WER with
  speaker- and recording-clustered bootstrap confidence
  intervals and Holm-corrected paired tests, a cross-model
  consensus classifier for reference artifacts, and a
  fine-tuning capacity study on a natively speaker-disjoint
  split replicated across six seeds at each of three model
  sizes.
keywords:
  - automatic speech recognition
  - word error rate
  - Indian English
  - benchmark
  - reproducibility
  - Whisper
  - evaluation
license: MIT
